{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784572807,"nonce":"2W+34ApRr3pV8+ewGPOcTdv+G9Q=","title":"Implements ADR-0057 §3 — environment-configurable requiredness of the manual dispatch reason. Reference the ADR for locked decisions.","message":"An Environment admin may require a **reason** for human dispatches into that environment. Enforced at the **admission gate** (beside `approvers`/`allowed_refs`, ADR-0037), NOT at the dispatch endpoint.\n\n- `ProtectionRules` gains `require_reason: bool` (`#[serde(default)]`, off = fail-open for existing environments). **Administer-scoped** to set, like the privilege whitelist (separation of duties). Persist it in the environment protection-rules storage (new migration).\n- Admission check: a run is blocked from deploying into a `require_reason` environment iff **`env.require_reason \u0026\u0026 trigger_kind ∈ {manual, api} \u0026\u0026 reason is empty`**. Push/PR/tag/release/cron/upstream are exempt (they carry their own intrinsic headline / are machine-initiated). The violation surfaces exactly like a missing approval.\n- Environment API surface (create/update) accepts and returns `require_reason`; regenerate OpenAPI.\n- Tests: admits() blocks an empty-reason manual run into a require_reason env; admits an api run WITH a reason; admits a push run regardless; unaffected when require_reason is off.\n\n\n- [ ] `ProtectionRules.require_reason` persists and round-trips through the Environment API (default off).\n- [ ] A manual/api dispatch with no reason into a require_reason environment is blocked at admission with a clear diagnostic (like a missing approval); with a reason it proceeds.\n- [ ] A push (or other non-manual/api) run into the same environment is NOT blocked.\n- [ ] Existing environments (require_reason unset) are unaffected — fail-open.\n- [ ] Setting require_reason requires the Administer capability.\n- [ ] `just check` + targeted `cargo test` green; OpenAPI regenerated.\n\n\n- [adr-0057] Manual/api dispatch reason input (slice C) — the rule enforces presence of the reason that slice C introduces.","files":null}]}